    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Adenoid cystic carcinoma&nbsp;shows cribriform islands and nests of basaloid cells, with pink basement membrane material as well as watery mucinous secretions. Both true&nbsp;lumens lined by luminal epithelial cells and pseudo lumens rimmed by myoepithelial cells are present within tumour islands. Tumour extends around an intraductal papilloma.</p>",
    "source": "Imported from 5th edition<br><br><p>SGH Pathology</p>",
